Have dinner with me?

257
00:13:09,355 --> 00:13:11,355
8:00?

258
00:13:11,391 --> 00:13:13,557
I'll relax.

259
00:13:24,237 --> 00:13:26,170
Well, what next?

260
00:13:30,076 --> 00:13:33,110
What an absolute creep!

261
00:13:34,347 --> 00:13:36,907
Please, Ben, he's not a creep.

262
00:13:37,850 --> 00:13:40,396
It's just that under pressure,

263
00:13:40,420 --> 00:13:43,421
his radio personality
slips into real life.

264
00:13:43,456 --> 00:13:44,822
He can't help it.

265
00:13:44,857 --> 00:13:46,824
He's a creep.

266
00:13:46,859 --> 00:13:48,392
What the matter with you?

267
00:13:48,427 --> 00:13:51,062
I've never seen you
this crazy over anybody.

268
00:13:51,097 --> 00:13:53,998
He's wrong for you.
I know it. I know!

269
00:13:54,033 --> 00:13:55,811
What do you think, you're
going to change him?

270
00:13:55,835 --> 00:13:56,878
Well, there's
always that chance.

271
00:13:56,902 --> 00:13:58,936
You can't change a rattlesnake

272
00:13:58,972 --> 00:14:02,340
into a pet rock you walk
around with in your pocket.

273
00:14:02,375 --> 00:14:04,108
Sooner or later,
he's going to bite you.

274
00:14:04,143 --> 00:14:06,610
It's probably sooner than later.

275
00:14:10,750 --> 00:14:13,517
<i>As, uh, most of you know,</i>

276
00:14:13,553 --> 00:14:17,522
I was a disc jockey at WBW
when Robby first signed on.

277
00:14:17,557 --> 00:14:21,258
I'll never forget
how excited he was

278
00:14:21,294 --> 00:14:23,527
the first time he sat
down in front of that mic.

279
00:14:23,562 --> 00:14:26,530
Or how truly grateful he was

280
00:14:26,566 --> 00:14:29,734
for any help that any one
of us could ever give him.

281
00:14:50,023 --> 00:14:52,790
Just had to see for myself.

282
00:14:52,825 --> 00:14:56,360
Be just like you to try
to pull a fast one on me.

283
00:16:05,864 --> 00:16:08,143
Mr. Lynch? Michelle Thomas.

284
00:16:08,167 --> 00:16:09,833
We had an appointment.

285
00:16:09,868 --> 00:16:11,168
What happened?

286
00:16:11,204 --> 00:16:13,604
Your client happened.

287
00:16:13,639 --> 00:16:15,206
Arthur did this?

288
00:16:15,241 --> 00:16:17,274
Yeah. Well, I told him
I was taking his show

289
00:16:17,310 --> 00:16:19,254
off the air until this
murder thing blew over,

290
00:16:19,278 --> 00:16:20,711
and he went nuts.

291
00:16:20,747 --> 00:16:23,047
He accused me of being
the one who framed him.

292
00:16:25,384 --> 00:16:26,494
Hey, wait a minute.

293
00:16:26,518 --> 00:16:28,318
I-I liked Robby Moore.

294
00:16:28,354 --> 00:16:30,232
I gave him his first big break.

295
00:16:30,256 --> 00:16:32,356
So you didn't mind
that he took that job

296
00:16:32,392 --> 00:16:33,624
with a rival station?

297
00:16:33,659 --> 00:16:36,627
Actually, I hated that.

298
00:16:36,662 --> 00:16:41,832
I hear he cost you close to
$600,000 in lost advertising.

299
00:16:41,867 --> 00:16:44,134
Yeah, well, I hated that, too.

300
00:16:44,169 --> 00:16:45,803
But I-I didn't kill him.

301
00:16:45,838 --> 00:16:48,038
I was at home, and I was alone!

302
00:16:49,676 --> 00:16:53,677
I've only killed Robby
Moore in my dreams.

303
00:16:53,712 --> 00:16:55,646
Arthur didn't believe you.

304
00:17:07,359 --> 00:17:09,960
Benj! Benj!

305
00:17:09,995 --> 00:17:12,162
Benjamin!

306
00:17:12,197 --> 00:17:14,832
Yo... Benj!

307
00:17:14,867 --> 00:17:16,500
Hi. Hi!

308
00:17:16,536 --> 00:17:17,568
Did I wake you?

309
00:17:17,603 --> 00:17:19,670
No. Good!

310
00:17:19,705 --> 00:17:22,506
Good. You know,
the other day I noticed

311
00:17:22,542 --> 00:17:24,920
you had a leak in your sink.

312
00:17:24,944 --> 00:17:26,677
About a drop a second.

313
00:17:26,712 --> 00:17:28,245
You know how much water

314
00:17:28,280 --> 00:17:30,525
that amounts to in a day's time?

315
00:17:30,549 --> 00:17:32,416
Enough to keep an entire

316
00:17:32,452 --> 00:17:35,085
Ethiopian family going. Hmm.

317
00:17:35,121 --> 00:17:37,054
7:00 in the morning,

318
00:17:37,090 --> 00:17:39,723
and you've already found
a way to give me guilt.

319
00:17:46,132 --> 00:17:48,032
What's that?

320
00:17:48,067 --> 00:17:49,366
I sent away.

321
00:17:49,402 --> 00:17:50,634
$39.50.

322
00:17:50,670 --> 00:17:52,903
It's the Mr. Handy Man.

323
00:17:52,939 --> 00:17:54,772
I'll fix that leak.

324
00:17:54,807 --> 00:17:57,641
Oh, no, that's too much
trouble. I'll call a plumber.

325
00:17:57,676 --> 00:17:59,643
Bite your tongue.

326
00:17:59,678 --> 00:18:01,045
20 bucks an hour?

327
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:03,413
Not while Ace Calhoun is around.

328
00:18:03,449 --> 00:18:06,350
And looky here, every
wrench known to man.

329
00:18:06,385 --> 00:18:08,953
Sockets, domestic and metric.

330
00:18:08,988 --> 00:18:10,654
And looky here,

331
00:18:10,689 --> 00:18:13,357
a spark plug
wrench for a Ferrari.

332
00:18:14,861 --> 00:18:16,494
You don't own a Ferrari.

333
00:18:16,529 --> 00:18:18,796
We don't know anybody
that owns a Ferrari.

334
00:18:18,831 --> 00:18:22,333
Well, it sets an example
for the other tools.

335
00:18:24,770 --> 00:18:27,071
Well, you know,
I do get restless

336
00:18:27,106 --> 00:18:28,906
in the mornings,

337
00:18:28,941 --> 00:18:30,974
what with Robby Moore gone.

338
00:18:32,645 --> 00:18:34,912
I tried to listen to
that other crumb.

339
00:18:34,947 --> 00:18:36,713
You know, the nasty one?

340
00:18:36,749 --> 00:18:39,183
Yeah, Arthur Saxon. Yeah.

341
00:18:39,218 --> 00:18:41,818
Boy, that guy really
gets under my skin.

342
00:18:41,854 --> 00:18:44,588
Sometimes, I'd like to
punch him right in the kisser.

343
00:18:44,623 --> 00:18:46,290
Mm-hmm.

344
00:18:46,325 --> 00:18:47,802
He's a suspect, you know.

345
00:18:47,826 --> 00:18:49,093
Yeah, I know.

346
00:18:49,128 --> 00:18:50,727
I'm defending him.

347
00:19:06,179 --> 00:19:08,813
Did a tornado come through here?

348
00:19:08,848 --> 00:19:11,481
May I help you, sir?

349
00:19:11,517 --> 00:19:14,451
Yeah. Is Leonard
Gilbert here yet?

350
00:19:16,022 --> 00:19:17,955
This way, sir.

351
00:19:38,211 --> 00:19:40,811
Um... Mr. Gilbert?

352
00:19:40,846 --> 00:19:42,613
Ben Matlock.

353
00:19:42,648 --> 00:19:44,348
This is your fault.

354
00:19:44,383 --> 00:19:45,882
If it weren't for you,

355
00:19:45,918 --> 00:19:48,486
that maniac would be
in jail where he belongs.

356
00:19:48,521 --> 00:19:51,822
This suit cost 800 bucks.

357
00:19:53,392 --> 00:19:55,512
Grape jelly doesn't come out.

358
00:19:57,463 --> 00:20:00,297
Arthur, uh... Arthur threw

359
00:20:00,332 --> 00:20:02,432
jelly on your suit?

360
00:20:04,570 --> 00:20:06,103
Let me get this straight.

361
00:20:06,138 --> 00:20:07,237
Arthur just walked in here

362
00:20:07,272 --> 00:20:08,973
and started throwing
jelly and stuff?

363
00:20:09,008 --> 00:20:10,073
That's not funny!

364
00:20:10,109 --> 00:20:11,442
I'm sorry.

365
00:20:11,477 --> 00:20:13,911
First, he just yelled at me.

366
00:20:13,947 --> 00:20:16,647
Accused me of framing him
for Robby Moore's murder.

367
00:20:16,682 --> 00:20:18,593
He didn't get
violent until I told him

368
00:20:18,617 --> 00:20:19,917
I was dropping him as a client.

369
00:20:19,952 --> 00:20:22,419
Oh. Oh, why-why was that?

370
00:20:22,454 --> 00:20:24,421
I'm an agent, Mr. Matlock.

371
00:20:24,456 --> 00:20:27,057
If a client goes down,
I go down with him.

372
00:20:27,092 --> 00:20:29,037
I need Arthur like I
need a hole in the head.

373
00:20:29,061 --> 00:20:30,427
Oh.

374
00:20:30,462 --> 00:20:32,696
WBW just laid him off.

375
00:20:32,731 --> 00:20:34,431
Ten percent of zero is zero.

376
00:20:34,466 --> 00:20:37,667
Oh. So, uh...

377
00:20:37,703 --> 00:20:40,371
you dropped Arthur like
Robby Moore dropped you?

378
00:20:42,441 --> 00:20:45,509
He decided that
he'd outgrown me.

379
00:20:45,544 --> 00:20:47,889
Accused me of stealing from him.

380
00:20:47,913 --> 00:20:51,048
How? He owed me money.

381
00:20:51,083 --> 00:20:53,618
That ungrateful rat.

382
00:20:53,653 --> 00:20:55,353
I bought him his first suit.

383
00:20:55,388 --> 00:20:57,187
Had his teeth capped.

384
00:20:57,223 --> 00:20:58,889
Paid for his nose job.

385
00:20:58,924 --> 00:21:01,692
Talked Marty Lynch into
giving him his first shot.

386
00:21:01,728 --> 00:21:03,894
Hell, I created him!

387
00:21:05,331 --> 00:21:06,975
And he just stabbed
you in the back.

388
00:21:06,999 --> 00:21:09,600
Yeah.

389
00:21:11,504 --> 00:21:14,505
Well, he's dead.

390
00:21:14,540 --> 00:21:16,507
I'm not.

391
00:21:16,542 --> 00:21:18,074
Arthur's going to fry.

392
00:21:18,110 --> 00:21:19,476
Things are looking up.

393
00:21:21,046 --> 00:21:23,180
Yeah.

394
00:21:23,216 --> 00:21:25,482
Yeah, yeah.

395
00:21:25,517 --> 00:21:28,152
Yeah, yeah...
Things are looking up.

396
00:21:28,187 --> 00:21:29,286
Yeah.

397
00:21:29,321 --> 00:21:30,654
I enjoyed talking with you.

398
00:21:30,690 --> 00:21:33,224
Yep. Yep. Yeah.

399
00:21:47,640 --> 00:21:49,906
Yeah. Make it quick, okay?

400
00:21:49,942 --> 00:21:52,209
Arthur! Security is on its way!

401
00:21:52,245 --> 00:21:54,123
So just don't do
anything you might regret.

402
00:21:54,147 --> 00:21:55,557
You lied to me,
Marty, didn't you?!

403
00:21:55,581 --> 00:21:56,691
You said you were home

404
00:21:56,715 --> 00:21:57,992
when Robby was
murdered, but you weren't.

405
00:21:58,016 --> 00:21:59,828
Who says I wasn't?
Your neighbor.

406
00:21:59,852 --> 00:22:01,452
Mrs. Krueger.

407
00:22:01,487 --> 00:22:03,498
Said she saw you
leave your house at 7:30.

408
00:22:03,522 --> 00:22:06,724
Moore was murdered at 7:45.

409
00:22:06,759 --> 00:22:08,169
Oh, come on. What does she know?

410
00:22:08,193 --> 00:22:09,505
The old bat's always
half in the bag.

411
00:22:09,529 --> 00:22:13,530
You wasted him, then
framed me. Didn't you?

412
00:22:13,565 --> 00:22:16,111
No, Arthur, please!
Don't, don't, Arthur!

413
00:22:16,135 --> 00:22:18,175
That's enough, Mr. Saxon!

414
00:22:23,642 --> 00:22:26,043
You are history!

415
00:22:36,889 --> 00:22:39,889
I don't get it, I don't
get it, I don't get it!

416
00:22:39,925 --> 00:22:43,327
You're my lawyer; you'd better
come up with something fast!

417
00:22:43,362 --> 00:22:45,874
What talent did
you rip that off?

418
00:22:45,898 --> 00:22:48,365
Okay, that's it!

419
00:22:48,401 --> 00:22:50,467
That's it.

420
00:22:52,137 --> 00:22:55,472
You'd better listen to me.

421
00:22:55,508 --> 00:22:58,275
You don't have a job.

422
00:22:58,310 --> 00:23:00,711
You don't have a defense.

423
00:23:00,746 --> 00:23:02,913
And in about a minute,
you won't have a lawyer.

424
00:23:02,949 --> 00:23:04,415
You can't quit on me now.

425
00:23:04,450 --> 00:23:05,916
I will in a heartbeat.

426
00:23:05,951 --> 00:23:08,385
Go ahead.

427
00:23:08,420 --> 00:23:09,954
I'll survive.

428
00:23:09,989 --> 00:23:12,055
And I'll come out on top.

429
00:23:12,091 --> 00:23:16,560
'Cause I've got talent
and I've got guts.

430
00:23:16,596 --> 00:23:18,428
And what more do I need?

431
00:23:18,464 --> 00:23:20,230
I'll tell you.

432
00:23:20,266 --> 00:23:23,233
You need some damn common sense!

433
00:23:23,269 --> 00:23:27,004
You need a jury that
wants to find you innocent.

434
00:23:27,039 --> 00:23:29,973
Not one that can't
wait to find you guilty.

435
00:23:30,008 --> 00:23:32,476
It's your job to
convince the jury.

436
00:23:32,511 --> 00:23:34,244
Yeah it's my job!

437
00:23:34,280 --> 00:23:37,347
You keep committing
mayhem, getting arrested,

438
00:23:37,382 --> 00:23:40,550
treating the whole world like
everybody's a fool but you,

439
00:23:40,585 --> 00:23:45,622
that jury's gonna find you
guilty, condemn you to death,

440
00:23:45,657 --> 00:23:47,691
the state's gonna
show you the chair,

441
00:23:47,726 --> 00:23:49,726
the guards are
gonna strap you in it,

442
00:23:49,761 --> 00:23:52,162
the chaplain is gonna
pray over your stupid head

443
00:23:52,198 --> 00:23:55,065
and I'm gonna pull
the switch personally

444
00:23:55,100 --> 00:23:56,466
and applaud. You got that?

445
00:24:14,053 --> 00:24:17,687
Hello, Ben, Arthur.

446
00:24:17,723 --> 00:24:21,624
I got the relief tape from WDW.

447
00:24:28,701 --> 00:24:31,568
You played this
relief tape every day?

448
00:24:31,604 --> 00:24:34,337
Right.

449
00:24:34,373 --> 00:24:37,675
But not exactly
at the same time.

450
00:24:37,710 --> 00:24:40,811
Well, whenever I got hungry.

451
00:24:40,846 --> 00:24:43,580
Sometimes earlier,
sometimes later.

452
00:24:43,615 --> 00:24:47,184
So, there was no way
any of our suspects

453
00:24:47,219 --> 00:24:50,521
could've known Arthur
was playing the tape.

454
00:24:53,225 --> 00:24:58,362
Unless something on the tape...

455
00:24:58,397 --> 00:25:00,997
tipped one of them off.

456
00:25:01,033 --> 00:25:02,599
But what would
we be listening for?

457
00:25:02,635 --> 00:25:03,915
I don't know.

458
00:25:06,171 --> 00:25:08,049
Aren't you gonna stay? No.

459
00:25:08,073 --> 00:25:10,140
You stay.

460
00:25:11,677 --> 00:25:14,611
If you hear anything
peculiar let me know.

461
00:25:29,128 --> 00:25:30,338
FEMALE CALLER: What can I do?

462
00:25:30,362 --> 00:25:31,706
Don't forget, sweet cheeks,

463
00:25:31,730 --> 00:25:34,198
a friend in need is a
pain in the B-U-T-T.

464
00:25:34,233 --> 00:25:37,267
Do unto others before
they do unto you.

465
00:25:37,302 --> 00:25:39,169
Yo! This is Arthur Saxon,

466
00:25:39,204 --> 00:25:41,304
lean, mean and better
than you deserve!

467
00:25:41,340 --> 00:25:45,208
WBW Radio, 98.6 FM, Atlanta.

468
00:25:45,244 --> 00:25:47,144
I'll rewind. No.

469
00:25:47,179 --> 00:25:50,013
I, uh, I can't listen anymore.

470
00:25:50,048 --> 00:25:51,916
I'm not hearing
anything important

471
00:25:51,951 --> 00:25:54,517
or peculiar.

472
00:25:54,553 --> 00:25:57,254
Maybe you need a break, Arthur.

473
00:25:57,289 --> 00:25:58,699
I'll make some fresh coffee.

474
00:25:58,723 --> 00:26:01,558
No! Throughout the show,
I've had a dozen cups already.

475
00:26:01,593 --> 00:26:03,126
I'm not gonna sleep for a month!

476
00:26:07,833 --> 00:26:12,402
Why don't, uh, you and I just
sit down over here and talk?

477
00:26:12,438 --> 00:26:14,916
We've been talking for hours.

478
00:26:14,940 --> 00:26:16,573
About the case.

479
00:26:16,608 --> 00:26:19,876
You're on trial for your life,
Arthur; the case is important.

480
00:26:19,911 --> 00:26:21,378
Mm-hmm.

481
00:26:37,663 --> 00:26:39,496
Better?

482
00:26:39,531 --> 00:26:41,765
Yeah.

483
00:26:41,801 --> 00:26:42,801
Mm.

484
00:26:47,906 --> 00:26:51,108
Arthur, you can't kiss me here.

485
00:26:51,143 --> 00:26:52,220
All right, I'll kiss you here.

486
00:26:52,244 --> 00:26:53,388
Arthur, no...

487
00:26:53,412 --> 00:26:55,256
You're making me very nervous.

488
00:26:55,280 --> 00:26:56,513
Since when?

489
00:26:56,548 --> 00:26:59,383
The cleaning crew comes
on Wednesday night.

490
00:26:59,418 --> 00:27:00,950
What time? 10:00.

491
00:27:00,986 --> 00:27:02,919
Got 23 minutes.

492
00:27:03,789 --> 00:27:06,256
Arthur!

493
00:27:06,292 --> 00:27:07,657
You are hopeless!

494
00:27:07,692 --> 00:27:09,292
What do you mean hopeless?

495
00:27:09,327 --> 00:27:11,962
You're the kind of man my
mother warned me about.

496
00:27:11,997 --> 00:27:14,798
A heartbreaker, love
them and leave them.

497
00:27:14,834 --> 00:27:17,234
A dangerous man.

498
00:27:21,640 --> 00:27:23,473
And you're my lawyer.

499
00:27:23,508 --> 00:27:25,175
So, I don't want to get you mad.

500
00:27:25,210 --> 00:27:28,311
I'm not mad.

501
00:27:28,346 --> 00:27:32,783
You're not?

502
00:27:32,818 --> 00:27:35,786
I never asked you for
a commitment, Arthur.

503
00:27:38,657 --> 00:27:41,158
At least once in
every woman's life,

504
00:27:41,193 --> 00:27:43,927
she should kiss a dangerous man.

505
00:27:55,407 --> 00:27:59,576
Maybe you and I
should get out of here.

506
00:27:59,611 --> 00:28:03,847
Go somewhere
quiet like my place.

507
00:28:10,289 --> 00:28:13,723
<i>Well, Pa, the rooster's
crowing and the sun's a-rising.</i>

508
00:28:13,759 --> 00:28:16,126
Where does the time go?

509
00:28:16,162 --> 00:28:20,664
Well, Ma, when we're jawin'
with our friends at WCPG,

510
00:28:20,699 --> 00:28:24,634
midnight to 6:00 is
just a spit in the wind.

511
00:28:24,670 --> 00:28:26,281
So, tell me nighty-night,

512
00:28:26,305 --> 00:28:30,040
this is Diedre Wallace
saying so long, ya'll.

513
00:28:30,075 --> 00:28:34,778
♪ <i>WCPG country
pickin' good time</i> ♪

514
00:28:34,814 --> 00:28:37,414
<i>93.4 on your FM dial.</i>

515
00:28:45,991 --> 00:28:49,393
Yeah, that's pretty funny stuff.

516
00:28:49,428 --> 00:28:53,763
I've been here three months,
nine days and six hours.

517
00:28:53,798 --> 00:28:56,032
You sound like
you don't like it.

518
00:28:56,068 --> 00:29:00,370
I used to be the top DJ at the
number one station in Atlanta.

519
00:29:00,406 --> 00:29:02,539
Now, I do
commercials for tractors

520
00:29:02,575 --> 00:29:04,541
and give pork belly reports.

521
00:29:04,577 --> 00:29:06,610
What do you think?

522
00:29:06,645 --> 00:29:10,413
Gee, on the air, you
sound like you love it.

523
00:29:10,449 --> 00:29:13,817
So, I'm a great actress.

524
00:29:13,852 --> 00:29:16,152
Hell, pays the rent.

525
00:29:16,187 --> 00:29:18,821
Huh. Huh.

526
00:29:20,192 --> 00:29:23,293
Yeah, uh... ooh!

527
00:29:23,328 --> 00:29:27,163
Oh, those were all taken
when I was back at WBW.

528
00:29:27,199 --> 00:29:30,500
Out here a celebrity
is the county fair winner

529
00:29:30,535 --> 00:29:32,336
of the hog calling contest.

530
00:29:32,371 --> 00:29:34,971
Oh.

531
00:29:35,006 --> 00:29:37,174
Is there a picture of
Robby Moore up there?

532
00:29:37,209 --> 00:29:40,710
No, but I don't have one of
the Ayatollah up there either.

533
00:29:42,781 --> 00:29:45,749
I don't want to be rude
to you, Mr. Matlock,

534
00:29:45,784 --> 00:29:49,185
but I am real beat and I
want to get out of here.

535
00:29:49,220 --> 00:29:51,888
I just want to go
home and go to bed.

536
00:29:51,924 --> 00:29:55,158
Is that what you do, uh, every
day after your show? Go home

537
00:29:55,193 --> 00:29:57,227
and go to bed?
Exciting, isn't it?

538
00:29:58,830 --> 00:30:02,466
Yeah, and that day I went
home and went to bed,

539
00:30:02,501 --> 00:30:06,336
and I got up around
2:00, put on the television

540
00:30:06,371 --> 00:30:09,940
and heard the news about Robby.

541
00:30:09,975 --> 00:30:12,542
I just marveled to think that

542
00:30:12,578 --> 00:30:16,846
there really is some
justice in this world after all.

543
00:30:28,894 --> 00:30:30,593
Paul.

544
00:30:30,629 --> 00:30:32,196
Where's Arthur?

545
00:30:32,231 --> 00:30:33,964
Oh, at home, I hope.

546
00:30:33,999 --> 00:30:35,465
Yeah, that little creep.

547
00:30:35,500 --> 00:30:36,799
Thinks he can come in here

548
00:30:36,835 --> 00:30:38,913
and wreck my office
and take a swing at me.

549
00:30:38,937 --> 00:30:41,939
Arthur's pretty hard
to take sometimes.

550
00:30:41,974 --> 00:30:45,008
Arthur's pretty hard to
take most of the time.

551
00:30:45,044 --> 00:30:48,078
But I think you're gonna want
to drop your assault charge.

552
00:30:48,113 --> 00:30:50,614
Ah... no, no, no.

553
00:30:50,649 --> 00:30:51,948
Not on your life!

554
00:30:51,984 --> 00:30:54,751
Don't think you can come
in here and lawyer-talk me

555
00:30:54,786 --> 00:30:57,153
out of seeing
Arthur in jail, uh-uh.

556
00:30:57,188 --> 00:31:02,358
Well, Mr. Lynch, you
lied about being home

557
00:31:02,394 --> 00:31:04,005
the morning Robby
Moore was murdered.

558
00:31:04,029 --> 00:31:06,395
What are you saying?

559
00:31:06,431 --> 00:31:10,133
I had a talk with
Mr. James T. Crosby.

560
00:31:10,169 --> 00:31:11,601
I believe you know Mr. Crosby.

561
00:31:11,637 --> 00:31:13,536
Yeah, I know him.

562
00:31:13,572 --> 00:31:15,906
So does your sound engineer.

563
00:31:15,941 --> 00:31:18,074
He saw you having
breakfast with him

564
00:31:18,110 --> 00:31:19,509
the morning of the murder.

565
00:31:19,545 --> 00:31:22,012
Yeah, well, we were,
uh, talking business.

566
00:31:22,047 --> 00:31:23,547
Big business.

567
00:31:23,582 --> 00:31:27,184
I understand James T. is
negotiating to buy your station.

568
00:31:27,219 --> 00:31:31,955
Mr. Matlock, please.

569
00:31:31,990 --> 00:31:35,358
If the wrong people
find out about this, the...

570
00:31:35,393 --> 00:31:38,028
That business deal can
go right down the tubes.

571
00:31:38,063 --> 00:31:40,931
So, that's the secret
you were trying to protect

572
00:31:40,966 --> 00:31:42,432
by saying you were at home.

573
00:31:42,468 --> 00:31:45,368
Well, yeah. I mean,
wouldn't you?!

574
00:31:45,403 --> 00:31:48,338
This, this deal
is worth millions!

575
00:31:49,874 --> 00:31:53,276
Look, you're not gonna tell
Arthur about this, are you?

576
00:31:53,311 --> 00:31:57,280
I mean, he's got a mouth
bigger than the Mississippi.

577
00:31:57,316 --> 00:31:59,615
He does, doesn't he?

578
00:32:04,490 --> 00:32:06,823
Arthur, I took a course

579
00:32:06,859 --> 00:32:09,493
on positive thinking,
and it changed my life.

580
00:32:09,528 --> 00:32:11,539
See, I used to think I was
weak and wimpy and...

581
00:32:11,563 --> 00:32:13,541
Yeah, well, you
still are, toad-breath.

582
00:32:13,565 --> 00:32:15,376
Take a course in skydiving
and call me from the cemetery.

583
00:32:15,400 --> 00:32:17,534
Anything? Not yet.

584
00:32:17,569 --> 00:32:19,146
Don't you keep a
record of who calls?

585
00:32:19,170 --> 00:32:22,272
Those yo-yos? Huh.

586
00:32:24,342 --> 00:32:29,513
Wait, remember you told me
that when a listener goes on the air,

587
00:32:29,548 --> 00:32:34,684
the station sends an official
WBW mug with your picture on it?

588
00:32:34,720 --> 00:32:36,886
Oh, so you do.

589
00:32:36,922 --> 00:32:39,122
You not only have
the names of the yoyos

590
00:32:39,157 --> 00:32:40,690
but their addresses.

591
00:32:40,725 --> 00:32:42,725
I'll call the station.

592
00:32:47,666 --> 00:32:50,445
Well, if everybody carried
a sawed-off shotgun,

593
00:32:50,469 --> 00:32:52,269
there'd be a lot less crime.

594
00:32:52,304 --> 00:32:55,405
Yeah, and a lot fewer
people, too, dork.

595
00:32:57,475 --> 00:33:02,145
Tsk. Well, there...

596
00:33:02,180 --> 00:33:09,019
There are 11 voices on that tape
and only ten mugs were sent out.

597
00:33:09,054 --> 00:33:12,321
Why?

598
00:33:12,357 --> 00:33:16,092
Someone could refuse a mug.

599
00:33:16,128 --> 00:33:19,895
One of these 11
people refused a mug.

600
00:33:19,931 --> 00:33:20,896
Which one?

601
00:33:20,932 --> 00:33:22,532
I don't know.

602
00:33:28,240 --> 00:33:30,607
Wait a minute.

603
00:33:30,642 --> 00:33:33,610
Yeah, I think I do know.

604
00:33:33,645 --> 00:33:34,911
It's that old guy that calls

605
00:33:34,946 --> 00:33:38,014
about twice a
month, Mr. Paranoid.

606
00:33:38,049 --> 00:33:40,850
Thinks everyone should
be armed and shoot to kill.

607
00:33:40,885 --> 00:33:42,585
Ha. Probably lives in a bunker

608
00:33:42,620 --> 00:33:44,553
and doesn't want
anyone to know where.

609
00:33:44,589 --> 00:33:46,156
Does he always refuse?

610
00:33:46,191 --> 00:33:48,358
Yeah, well, I guess so.

611
00:33:51,163 --> 00:33:54,008
Well, if everybody carried
a sawed-off shotgun,

612
00:33:54,032 --> 00:33:55,798
there'd be a lot less crime.

613
00:33:55,834 --> 00:33:57,712
Yeah, and a lot fewer
people, too, dork.

614
00:33:57,736 --> 00:33:59,902
Oh, come on, man, this
is a big waste of time.

615
00:33:59,938 --> 00:34:02,639
Wait, wait a minute, wait.

616
00:34:02,674 --> 00:34:05,342
Well, if everybody carried
a sawed-off shotgun,

617
00:34:05,377 --> 00:34:07,577
there'd be a lot less crime.

618
00:34:07,612 --> 00:34:13,583
This is the person who
killed Robby Moore.

619
00:34:14,719 --> 00:34:16,019
How do you know?

620
00:34:16,054 --> 00:34:18,354
I just know.

621
00:34:18,389 --> 00:34:20,656
I can't prove it yet.

622
00:34:34,339 --> 00:34:36,306
Hmm.

623
00:34:36,341 --> 00:34:37,640
Hmm.

624
00:34:37,675 --> 00:34:39,242
Some deal, huh? Yeah.

625
00:34:39,277 --> 00:34:42,678
Station built him a studio
right in his own house.

626
00:34:42,714 --> 00:34:44,754
Must've wanted him
pretty badly. Yeah.

627
00:34:54,493 --> 00:34:56,559
Hmm.

628
00:34:56,594 --> 00:34:59,696
Pretty nice-looking
fellow, wasn't he?

629
00:34:59,731 --> 00:35:01,998
Mm. You know.

630
00:35:18,016 --> 00:35:22,919
Uh, you used to
be a-a disc jockey

631
00:35:22,954 --> 00:35:26,356
at, uh, station WBW

632
00:35:26,391 --> 00:35:29,025
along with Arthur Saxon and
Robby Moore, is that right?

633
00:35:29,060 --> 00:35:30,559
Yes, I was.

634
00:35:30,595 --> 00:35:34,030
But you were... let go.

635
00:35:34,065 --> 00:35:36,866
Fired, Mr. Matlock, yes.

636
00:35:36,901 --> 00:35:39,602
Didn't the listeners
like your program?

637
00:35:39,638 --> 00:35:42,539
Robby Moore didn't like me.

638
00:35:42,574 --> 00:35:45,086
He was jealous,
so he had me fired.

639
00:35:45,110 --> 00:35:46,776
Oh.

640
00:35:46,811 --> 00:35:50,413
But after a while, you
found another position

641
00:35:50,449 --> 00:35:52,548
at station WCPG?

642
00:35:52,584 --> 00:35:55,351
Voice of the Boonies, yeah.

643
00:35:55,386 --> 00:35:57,386
Same pay?

644
00:35:57,422 --> 00:35:58,855
Hardly.

645
00:35:58,890 --> 00:36:00,130
Much less.

646
00:36:00,159 --> 00:36:05,462
So much less in fact
that the, um, the bank,

647
00:36:05,497 --> 00:36:07,964
uh, repossessed
the home you bought.

648
00:36:08,000 --> 00:36:10,333
I lost my home, yes.

649
00:36:10,368 --> 00:36:16,706
Well, with Robby Moore dead

650
00:36:16,741 --> 00:36:20,877
and, uh, Arthur Saxon
out of the running,

651
00:36:20,913 --> 00:36:24,981
why, uh, maybe something will
come up for you back at WBW.

652
00:36:25,017 --> 00:36:26,316
Objection!

653
00:36:26,351 --> 00:36:28,863
I fail to see the
relevancy of any of this.

654
00:36:28,887 --> 00:36:30,731
It goes to motive, Your Honor.

655
00:36:30,755 --> 00:36:34,123
Your Honor, the people have
already established motive.

656
00:36:34,159 --> 00:36:36,025
Uh, for my client, yes,

657
00:36:36,061 --> 00:36:38,995
but not for the person who
actually killed Robby Moore.

658
00:36:39,030 --> 00:36:40,396
Am I correct in assuming

659
00:36:40,431 --> 00:36:43,800
you know better than to make
an allegation without proof?

660
00:36:43,835 --> 00:36:46,047
Uh, yes, ma'am, I'm
going for that now.

661
00:36:46,071 --> 00:36:47,971
Proceed.

662
00:36:48,006 --> 00:36:49,673
Thank you.

663
00:36:49,708 --> 00:36:53,610
Uh... Uh, when you were at WBW,

664
00:36:53,645 --> 00:36:56,946
did you ever, uh, send
your car out to be washed?

665
00:36:56,982 --> 00:36:58,448
Yes.

666
00:36:58,483 --> 00:36:59,682
How'd you do that?

667
00:36:59,718 --> 00:37:02,786
I would call an attendant,

668
00:37:02,821 --> 00:37:04,154
he'd take the car someplace,

669
00:37:04,189 --> 00:37:05,800
have it washed
and bring it back.

670
00:37:05,824 --> 00:37:07,423
Where'd he get the key?

671
00:37:07,458 --> 00:37:09,925
I kept a spare in the
glove compartment.

672
00:37:09,961 --> 00:37:13,662
Just like all the other people

673
00:37:13,698 --> 00:37:15,064
who worked at the station?

674
00:37:15,100 --> 00:37:18,768
A lot of people did
that, I believe, yes.

675
00:37:18,804 --> 00:37:25,541
A witness testified that
she saw Arthur Saxon's car

676
00:37:25,577 --> 00:37:30,146
racing away from
Robby Moore's house

677
00:37:30,182 --> 00:37:32,882
right after the murder
had been committed.

678
00:37:32,918 --> 00:37:34,818
She didn't see who was driving,

679
00:37:34,853 --> 00:37:38,555
but you knew about the key.

680
00:37:38,590 --> 00:37:40,924
You knew where
Arthur parked his car.

681
00:37:40,959 --> 00:37:44,226
So, I submit, it was you

682
00:37:44,262 --> 00:37:46,563
who was driving
the car that morning.

683
00:37:46,598 --> 00:37:49,498
I was at home, sleeping.

684
00:37:49,534 --> 00:37:51,134
No, I don't think so.

685
00:37:51,169 --> 00:37:53,903
No, I don't think so.

686
00:37:55,674 --> 00:37:58,820
Well, if everybody carried
a sawed-off shotgun,

687
00:37:58,844 --> 00:38:01,778
there'd be a lot less crime.

688
00:38:01,813 --> 00:38:03,279
Know who that was?

689
00:38:03,315 --> 00:38:05,581
I have no idea.

690
00:38:05,617 --> 00:38:08,451
That's one of the voices

691
00:38:08,486 --> 00:38:11,554
on the relief tape we've
heard so much about.

692
00:38:11,590 --> 00:38:13,723
The one the prosecution says

693
00:38:13,758 --> 00:38:18,328
that Arthur was playing
when he was not on the air.

694
00:38:19,431 --> 00:38:20,563
So?

695
00:38:20,598 --> 00:38:24,300
All right, what about this?

696
00:38:26,171 --> 00:38:30,673
Well, Ma, when we're jawin'
with our friends at WCPG,

697
00:38:30,708 --> 00:38:33,910
midnight to 6:00 is
just a spit in the wind.

698
00:38:33,945 --> 00:38:36,545
That's me on WCPG.

699
00:38:36,581 --> 00:38:37,980
That's hardly a secret.

700
00:38:38,016 --> 00:38:44,921
No, no, the secret
is... that you are also

701
00:38:44,956 --> 00:38:48,358
our shotgun-carrying
Mr. Clemens.

702
00:38:48,393 --> 00:38:50,326
That's ridiculous, I am not.

703
00:38:52,230 --> 00:38:56,799
You're a very, very
talented woman.

704
00:38:56,834 --> 00:38:59,936
And I have a confession to make.

705
00:38:59,971 --> 00:39:01,771
I'm a fan.

706
00:39:02,874 --> 00:39:05,274
I listen to, on the radio,

707
00:39:05,309 --> 00:39:08,845
classical music or
country and western.

708
00:39:08,880 --> 00:39:11,047
I'll go from Mozart and Brahms

709
00:39:11,082 --> 00:39:15,217
right to Eddy Arnold,
and I listen to you.

710
00:39:15,253 --> 00:39:16,352
You're very talented.

711
00:39:16,387 --> 00:39:18,487
You do all those voices.

712
00:39:18,522 --> 00:39:21,257
You do them so well,
no one would ever know

713
00:39:21,292 --> 00:39:26,028
that you are not all those
people except for one thing.

714
00:39:26,064 --> 00:39:28,297
Where are you from originally?

715
00:39:28,332 --> 00:39:30,500
Arkansas.

716
00:39:30,535 --> 00:39:31,901
That's it.

717
00:39:31,936 --> 00:39:33,436
That's it.

718
00:39:35,106 --> 00:39:39,242
Listening to you all this time,

719
00:39:39,277 --> 00:39:43,046
and I just now figured it out.

720
00:39:43,081 --> 00:39:45,147
It's the "R" sound.

721
00:39:45,183 --> 00:39:48,718
People from Arkansas
often add a little

722
00:39:48,753 --> 00:39:51,387
"R" sound to their words.

723
00:39:51,423 --> 00:39:52,489
"Arkansawr."

724
00:39:52,524 --> 00:39:54,757
"Sawred-off shotgun."

725
00:39:54,792 --> 00:39:59,061
It's a beautiful accent,
but it's unmistakable.

726
00:39:59,096 --> 00:40:02,698
And there your voice is,

727
00:40:02,734 --> 00:40:06,235
on Arthur's relief tape.

728
00:40:06,270 --> 00:40:09,572
Why would I call
Arthur's show, hmm?

729
00:40:09,608 --> 00:40:12,408
Well, you called
him late Monday,

730
00:40:12,443 --> 00:40:18,447
knowing it would be taped
and played on Tuesday morning.

731
00:40:18,483 --> 00:40:22,184
So, on Tuesday morning,
you got in Arthur's car,

732
00:40:22,220 --> 00:40:24,621
drove over to Robby
Moore's house,

733
00:40:24,656 --> 00:40:29,959
turned on the radio and
waited till you heard your voice,

734
00:40:29,995 --> 00:40:33,062
knowing that Arthur
would not be on the air live

735
00:40:33,098 --> 00:40:35,298
and therefore would
not have an alibi.

736
00:40:35,333 --> 00:40:38,467
And you went in the house

737
00:40:38,502 --> 00:40:42,404
with the gun you had
taken from Arthur's party,

738
00:40:42,441 --> 00:40:46,309
and shot your old
nemesis to death.

739
00:40:46,344 --> 00:40:49,445
All right, yes, I
called Arthur's show.

740
00:40:49,480 --> 00:40:52,315
I did it as a joke to
see if I could fool him,

741
00:40:52,350 --> 00:40:53,883
which I did,

742
00:40:53,918 --> 00:40:56,886
but that hardly means
that I killed Robby Moore.

743
00:40:56,922 --> 00:41:00,489
Just one more
thing, one more thing.

744
00:41:00,525 --> 00:41:05,395
I understand that you're
a big fan of John Lennon.

745
00:41:05,430 --> 00:41:07,697
Yes, I am.

746
00:41:07,732 --> 00:41:10,165
Did you ever meet
him personally?

747
00:41:10,202 --> 00:41:11,401
Once.

748
00:41:11,436 --> 00:41:13,069
Where was that?

749
00:41:13,104 --> 00:41:15,271
He was on a promotional
tour of Atlanta,

750
00:41:15,307 --> 00:41:18,407
and he stopped by some
of the major radio stations.

751
00:41:18,443 --> 00:41:19,909
Ah.

752
00:41:21,846 --> 00:41:24,713
Autograph that was on a picture.

753
00:41:24,749 --> 00:41:31,887
"To all my friends at WBW,
now and forever, John."

754
00:41:35,527 --> 00:41:38,194
That's a valuable photograph.

755
00:41:38,229 --> 00:41:42,632
Mr. Lynch told me that he more
or less gave you that picture.

756
00:41:42,667 --> 00:41:45,368
Put on your wall
behind your desk.

757
00:41:45,403 --> 00:41:47,303
Since you were such a big fan,

758
00:41:47,339 --> 00:41:49,772
he figured you'd
take the best care of it,

759
00:41:49,807 --> 00:41:53,142
but when you were fired,
gone, the picture stayed.

760
00:41:53,177 --> 00:41:54,544
I guess Robby Moore thought

761
00:41:54,579 --> 00:41:56,613
it would look good
on his wall, too.

762
00:41:56,648 --> 00:41:58,848
Whatever Robby
wanted, Robby got.

763
00:42:00,485 --> 00:42:02,117
Hmm.

764
00:42:02,153 --> 00:42:04,119
Maybe you can explain something.

765
00:42:04,155 --> 00:42:07,890
Um, this, uh...

766
00:42:07,926 --> 00:42:12,261
This is a publicity still
that Robby Moore sent out.

767
00:42:12,296 --> 00:42:14,063
See, that's Robby
there in his studio,

768
00:42:14,098 --> 00:42:15,765
and those are the
pictures on the wall.

769
00:42:15,800 --> 00:42:17,466
You see the picture there?

770
00:42:17,501 --> 00:42:19,468
Of John Lennon?

771
00:42:19,503 --> 00:42:22,872
Yeah, now...

772
00:42:22,908 --> 00:42:25,742
this is the photograph the
police took after the murder.

773
00:42:25,777 --> 00:42:27,410
There's Robby... poor Robby...

774
00:42:27,445 --> 00:42:29,579
And the pictures.

775
00:42:29,614 --> 00:42:32,548
Picture of John Lennon's gone.

776
00:42:32,583 --> 00:42:34,450
And here's why.

777
00:42:38,222 --> 00:42:39,589
It's here in my hand.

778
00:42:39,624 --> 00:42:43,192
The police retrieved it

779
00:42:43,227 --> 00:42:47,930
from the wall behind
your desk this morning.

780
00:42:47,966 --> 00:42:52,468
You wanted this picture so badly

781
00:42:52,504 --> 00:42:55,371
that you took it
after you shot him.

782
00:42:55,406 --> 00:42:57,573
You figured the people
at that little station

783
00:42:57,608 --> 00:43:00,676
would never notice.

784
00:43:00,711 --> 00:43:03,546
And you were right, they didn't.

785
00:43:05,549 --> 00:43:10,319
I don't know much about rock
and roll music and don't care,

786
00:43:10,354 --> 00:43:15,725
but I know that John
Lennon was a famous man.

787
00:43:15,760 --> 00:43:17,426
And I noticed.

788
00:43:26,070 --> 00:43:29,771
We find the
defendant not guilty.

789
00:43:29,807 --> 00:43:33,843
A not guilty verdict is
entered in the record.

790
00:43:33,878 --> 00:43:36,779
Court is adjourned.

791
00:43:42,320 --> 00:43:45,822
So, I guess nice guys
don't always finish last, huh?

792
00:43:45,857 --> 00:43:51,260
Mr. Saxon, with any luck,

793
00:43:51,295 --> 00:43:53,663
I'll never see you again.

794
00:44:04,876 --> 00:44:06,242
You still at it?

795
00:44:06,277 --> 00:44:08,144
Oh, the faucet's fixed.

796
00:44:08,179 --> 00:44:10,913
I found some ham and
cheese in your ice box,

797
00:44:10,949 --> 00:44:13,683
and I thought I'd better
finish it before it goes bad.

798
00:44:13,718 --> 00:44:16,886
Oh, good.

799
00:44:16,921 --> 00:44:18,354
How's Arthur Saxon?

800
00:44:18,389 --> 00:44:19,566
Oh, disgusting.

801
00:44:19,590 --> 00:44:22,358
Did you say you
finished the sink?

802
00:44:22,393 --> 00:44:23,726
Yeah, let's give her a whirl!

803
00:44:23,761 --> 00:44:25,427
Okay.

804
00:44:25,462 --> 00:44:26,929
All right, now.

805
00:44:26,964 --> 00:44:29,131
When I turn the
water on down here,

806
00:44:29,167 --> 00:44:30,900
you turn it on up there, okay?

807
00:44:30,935 --> 00:44:31,967
Okay!

808
00:44:32,003 --> 00:44:36,505
In five, four, three, two, one!

9999
